Data licence — data-retrieved releases
======================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code in this repository. It does not
cover the data published in this repository's releases, and no licence is
granted over that data.

The retrieved-data files are raw scrapes. Each one holds the responses a venue
website or ticketing platform gave us, stored close to verbatim — the site's
own JSON payloads, page content and listing text — so that the transform stage
can be re-run and debugged without hitting the source site again. They are an
internal build artifact, published here because the pipeline runs in the open,
not as a dataset offered for reuse.

That content belongs to the venues and platforms it came from. Clusterflick
holds no rights in it and grants none. Nothing here is offered under any
licence, and republishing it is a matter between you and the source site.

Concretely:

  * No licence is granted over these releases, of any kind.
  * There are no schema guarantees. Every file's shape is whatever the source
    site happened to return, and changes whenever that site changes.
  * There is no warranty and no guarantee of accuracy, availability or
    continuity. Releases can stop, be deleted or be restructured at any time.

